## Hands-On: Temperature Converter 🌡️

:::{.fragment}
**Your Task**: Create a function to convert Celsius to Fahrenheit

**Formula**: `F = (C × 9/5) + 32`
:::

:::{.fragment}
**Try it yourself first!** Then see solution on next slide...
:::

---

## Solution: Temperature Converter

```sql
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION celsius_to_fahrenheit(celsius NUMERIC)
RETURNS NUMERIC AS $$
DECLARE
    fahrenheit NUMERIC;
BEGIN
    -- Check for absolute zero violation (below -273.15°C)
    IF celsius < -273.15 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION 'Temperature cannot be below absolute zero!';
    END IF;
    
    -- Apply formula: F = (C × 9/5) + 32
    fahrenheit := (celsius * 9.0 / 5.0) + 32;
    
    -- Round to 2 decimal places
    RETURN ROUND(fahrenheit, 2);
END;
$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql;
```

### Test it:
```sql
SELECT celsius_to_fahrenheit(0);      -- 32.00 (freezing point)
SELECT celsius_to_fahrenheit(100);    -- 212.00 (boiling point)
SELECT celsius_to_fahrenheit(-40);    -- -40.00 (C and F meet!)
SELECT celsius_to_fahrenheit(25);     -- 77.00 (room temperature)
```

