## Real-World Example: Library System 📚

```sql
-- Check if book is available
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION is_book_available(book_id INTEGER)
RETURNS BOOLEAN AS $$
DECLARE
    copies_total INTEGER;
    copies_out INTEGER;
    available INTEGER;
BEGIN
    -- Get book inventory
    SELECT total_copies, checked_out_copies
    INTO copies_total, copies_out
    FROM books
    WHERE id = book_id;
    
    -- Check if book exists
    IF copies_total IS NULL THEN
        RAISE NOTICE 'Book ID % not found', book_id;
        RETURN FALSE;
    END IF;
    
    -- Calculate available copies
    available := copies_total - copies_out;
    
    -- Log for debugging
    RAISE NOTICE 'Book %: % total, % out, % available', 
                 book_id, copies_total, copies_out, available;
    
    RETURN available > 0;
END;
$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql;
```

### Usage Example:
```sql
-- Check before attempting checkout
SELECT is_book_available(101);  
-- NOTICE: Book 101: 5 total, 3 out, 2 available
-- Result: TRUE

-- Use in a WHERE clause
SELECT title, author 
FROM books 
WHERE is_book_available(id) = TRUE;
```

---

## Real-World Example: Check Out Book

```sql
CREATE OR REPLACE PROCEDURE checkout_book(
    p_book_id INTEGER,
    p_user_id INTEGER
)
AS $$
DECLARE
    v_book_title TEXT;
    v_due_date DATE;
BEGIN
    -- Validate inputs
    IF p_book_id IS NULL OR p_user_id IS NULL THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION 'Book ID and User ID are required';
    END IF;
    
    -- Check if book is available
    IF NOT is_book_available(p_book_id) THEN
        SELECT title INTO v_book_title 
        FROM books WHERE id = p_book_id;
        RAISE EXCEPTION 'Book "%" is not available', v_book_title;
    END IF;
    
    -- Check if user already has this book
    IF EXISTS (
        SELECT 1 FROM checkouts 
        WHERE book_id = p_book_id 
        AND user_id = p_user_id 
        AND return_date IS NULL
    ) THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION 'User already has this book checked out';
    END IF;
    
    -- Calculate due date (2 weeks from today)
    v_due_date := CURRENT_DATE + INTERVAL '14 days';
    
    -- Create checkout record
    INSERT INTO checkouts (book_id, user_id, checkout_date, due_date)
    VALUES (p_book_id, p_user_id, CURRENT_DATE, v_due_date);
    
    -- Update book inventory
    UPDATE books
    SET checked_out_copies = checked_out_copies + 1
    WHERE id = p_book_id;
    
    -- Get book title for confirmation message
    SELECT title INTO v_book_title FROM books WHERE id = p_book_id;
    
    RAISE NOTICE 'Book "%" checked out successfully! Due: %', 
                 v_book_title, v_due_date;
END;
$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql;
```

### How to use it:
```sql
CALL checkout_book(101, 5);
-- NOTICE: Book "Database Design" checked out successfully! Due: 2025-11-20

-- Error handling in action:
CALL checkout_book(101, 5);  -- Try to checkout same book again
-- ERROR: User already has this book checked out
```

---

## Common Patterns Cheat Sheet 📋

:::{.fragment}
**Pattern 1: Simple Calculation**
```sql
CREATE FUNCTION pattern(input TYPE) RETURNS TYPE AS $$
BEGIN
    RETURN input * some_formula;
END;
$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql;
```
:::

:::{.fragment}
**Pattern 2: Lookup & Return**
```sql
CREATE FUNCTION pattern(id INT) RETURNS TYPE AS $$
DECLARE result TYPE;
BEGIN
    SELECT column INTO result FROM table WHERE id = id;
    RETURN COALESCE(result, default_value);
END;
$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql;
```
:::

:::{.fragment}
**Pattern 3: Validation Function**
```sql
CREATE FUNCTION is_valid_pattern(value TYPE) RETURNS BOOLEAN AS $$
BEGIN
    IF value meets_criteria THEN
        RETURN TRUE;
    END IF;
    RETURN FALSE;
END;
$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql;
```
:::

:::{.fragment}
**Pattern 4: Update Procedure**
```sql
CREATE PROCEDURE update_pattern(id INT, new_value TYPE) AS $$
BEGIN
    -- Validate
    IF NOT is_valid(new_value) THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION 'Invalid value';
    END IF;
    -- Update
    UPDATE table SET column = new_value WHERE id = id;
END;
$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql;
```
:::

---

## Summary: Key Takeaways 📝

:::{.fragment}
✅ **Functions return values**, procedures perform actions
:::

:::{.fragment}
✅ **Parameters** let you pass in different inputs
:::

:::{.fragment}
✅ **Variables** store temporary calculations (use `:=`)
:::


:::{.fragment}
✅ **Always validate** your inputs (NULL checks, range checks)
:::

:::{.fragment}
✅ **Use meaningful names** with prefixes (`p_` for parameters, `v_` for variables)
:::

:::{.fragment}
✅ **Test incrementally** - build and test step by step
:::

:::{.fragment}
✅ **Add error handling** - RAISE NOTICE, WARNING, or EXCEPTION
:::



